{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Back up /srv/inventory/data from node2 into dated archives under /var/backups/inventory on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A manual service run produced inventory-2026-10-04.tar.gz on node1 with root-only permissions and valid tar integrity. A verification file from node2 was present in the archive with an identical SHA-256 hash, directly demonstrating the node2-to-node1 data path. Subsequent clean backups also succeeded.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1c9352d13bb34e0d","cmd-40a1547ef53d44b7","cmd-ea1781dcf3c94aed","cmd-daf0b7bf0b2b45c6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Run the inventory backup every night.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The systemd timer is enabled, active, persistent, and scheduled daily at 02:15 with up to 15 minutes randomized delay. The backup service succeeded manually and again after both nodes were restarted; the timer remained enabled and active after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5b8108b17a9b4224","cmd-274c9a7e4a8d44cd","cmd-d9e7d4ce1d454824","cmd-3a6984c917e94298","cmd-daf0b7bf0b2b45c6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Retain backups for the last seven days.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed backup script deletes matching dated archives with mtime greater than six days, retaining the current daily archive plus the preceding six daily intervals. A deliberately eight-day-old archive was removed by a successful backup run, while the current archive remained and no temporary archive was left behind.","evidence_ids":["cmd-86f5c8690c0d41c2","cmd-ea1781dcf3c94aed","cmd-daf0b7bf0b2b45c6"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with that platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after implementation and restart. The solution uses already available OpenSSH, tar, find, and systemd facilities, and final package-health checks passed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a163c8c689cd4ea7","cmd-bbe70683546b44d5","cmd-daf0b7bf0b2b45c6","cmd-61a1f3c14ec64710","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:before_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary state-changing mutations were identified. Creating the absent source directory, restricted transfer account, SSH credentials, backup scripts, destination, service, and timer directly supported the task. The verification marker and stale retention-test archive were bounded evidence artifacts and were removed. The initially insufficient forced-command policy was corrected after a read-only rejection test; the correction contributed directly to the final restricted transfer design. Restart mutations were required by the provider evidence protocol. Final observations show no failed units, no added listeners, no temporary verification files, and healthy package state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cc7c111b71b94a7c","cmd-476a17bce75e4b32","cmd-5b8108b17a9b4224","cmd-1c9352d13bb34e0d","cmd-86f5c8690c0d41c2","cmd-92e02637c1994301","cmd-ea1781dcf3c94aed","cmd-44d7de9974584ecb","cmd-8e21d113c5684d47","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The backup path was proven with matching source and restored hashes, nightly automation is active and restart-persistent, eight-day-old data was removed under the seven-day policy, and both nodes retained their original OS and kernel. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart backup behavior were directly observed and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["The evidence does not include waiting for an actual overnight timer firing; nightly operation is supported by the active schedule, successful direct service executions, and post-restart persistence.","Retention behavior was tested with one eight-day-old artifact rather than a naturally accumulated seven-day archive set."]}
